<strong>:</strong></em>Prostate.Seminal vesicle.<em><strong>InvestigationHSA:72 hours’ abstinence.Endocrinology:If count &lt;5M/ml.Testosterone, FSH, LH.Prolactin.TSH if,Reduced libido.Impotence.Genetic screening:Severe oligo/AzoospermiaConcentration &lt;15M/mlTotal count &lt;5M/ejaculate.Karyotyping:Most frequently detected sex chromosomal abnormality Klinefelter 11% in azoospermia.Microdeletions:10 – 15% with azo.2 – 10% with severe oligo.AZFc – good prognosis with surgical retrieval.AZFa, AZFb: poor prognosis of ART.Imaging:Testicular USG:If abnormality detected on examination.Renal USG:If absence of VAS, 30% association with Renal Abnormality.Testicular Biopsy:Open/percutaneousSevere oligo/AzoospermiaICSI.InvestigationHSA:72 hours’ abstinence.Endocrinology:If count &lt;5M/ml.Testosterone, FSH, LH.Prolactin.TSH if,Reduced libido.Impotence.Genetic screening:Severe oligo/AzoospermiaConcentration &lt;15M/mlTotal count &lt;5M/ejaculate.Karyotyping:Most frequently detected sex chromosomal abnormality Klinefelter 11% in azoospermia.Microdeletions:10 – 15% with azo.2 – 10% with severe oligo.AZFc – good prognosis with surgical retrieval.AZFa, AZFb: poor prognosis of ART.Imaging:Testicular USG:If abnormality detected on examination.Renal USG:If absence of VAS, 30% association with Renal Abnormality.Testicular Biopsy:Open/percutaneousSevere oligo/AzoospermiaICSI.</strong></em><strong>Investigation</strong><strong>HSA:</strong>72 hours’ abstinence.<strong>Endocrinology:</strong>If count &lt;5M/ml.Testosterone, FSH, LH.Prolactin.TSH if,Reduced libido.Impotence.<strong>Genetic screening:</strong><em><strong>Severe oligo/Azo</strong></em><em><strong>ospermia</strong></em>Concentration &lt;15M/mlTotal count &lt;5M/ejaculate.<em><strong>Karyotyping:</strong></em>Most frequently detected sex chromosomal abnormality Klinefelter 11% in azoospermia.<em><strong>Microdeletions:</strong></em>10 – 15% with azo.2 – 10% with severe oligo.<strong>AZF</strong><strong>c</strong><strong> </strong>– good prognosis with surgical retrieval.<strong>AZFa</strong><strong>,</strong><strong> AZFb:</strong> poor prognosis of ART.<strong>Imaging:</strong>Testicular USG:If abnormality detected on examination.Renal USG:If absence of VAS, 30% association with Renal Abnormality.<strong>Testicular Biopsy:</strong>Open/percutaneousSevere oligo/AzoospermiaICSI.<strong>Investigation</strong><strong>HSA:</strong>72 hours’ abstinence.<strong>Endocrinology:</strong>If count &lt;5M/ml.Testosterone, FSH, LH.Prolactin.TSH if,Reduced libido.Impotence.<strong>Genetic screening:</strong><em><strong>Severe oligo/Azo</strong></em><em><strong>ospermia</strong></em>Concentration &lt;15M/mlTotal count &lt;5M/ejaculate.<em><strong>Karyotyping:</strong></em>Most frequently detected sex chromosomal abnormality Klinefelter 11% in azoospermia.<em><strong>Microdeletions:</strong></em>10 – 15% with azo.2 – 10% with severe oligo.<strong>AZF</strong><strong>c</strong><strong> </strong>– good prognosis with surgical retrieval.<strong>AZFa</strong><strong>,</strong><strong> AZFb:</strong> poor prognosis of ART.<strong>Imaging:</strong>Testicular USG:If abnormality detected on examination.Renal USG:If absence of VAS, 30% association with Renal Abnormality.<strong>Testicular Biopsy:</strong>Open/percutaneousSevere oligo/AzoospermiaICSI.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>History</strong></h3>
<h3><em><strong>Medical:</strong></em></h3>
<ul><li>Pyrexia.</li><li>Systemic disease,</li><li>DM, SLE.</li><li>Genetic</li><li>Klinefelter.</li><li>Cystic fibrosis</li></ul>
<h3><em><strong>Surgical:</strong></em></h3>
<ul><li>Undescended</li><li>Testes.</li><li>Hernia repair.</li><li>Testicular trauma</li><li>torsion.</li><li><em><strong>Standing positionStanding position</strong></em>Standing positionStanding positionPelvic, bladder,</li><li>Retroperitoneal</li><li>Surgery.</li></ul>
<h3><em><strong>Sexual history:</strong></em></h3>
<ul><li>Erection/ejaculation</li><li>Frequency of</li><li>Intercourse.</li></ul>
<h3><em><strong>Medicine:</strong></em></h3>
<ul><li>Nitrofurantoin – Methotrexate</li><li>Cimetidine – colchicine</li><li>Spironolactone – amiodarone</li><li>Sulfasalazine – Antidepressants.</li><li>Phenothiazine’s.</li><li>alpha – Blockers, chemotherapy.</li></ul>
<h3><em><strong>Social history:</strong></em></h3>
<ul><li>Alcohol, drugs.</li><li>Smoking.</li><li>Ionizing radiation.</li><li>Chronic heat.</li><li>aniline dye Pesticide.</li><li>Lead exposure.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Treatment:</strong></h3>
<ul><li><strong>Medical:</strong></li><li>CAH.</li><li>Hypogonadotropic – hypogonadism.</li><li>Hyperprolactinemia.</li><li>GnRH A or Gonadotrophins.</li><li>No role in idiopathic.</li><li><strong>surgical:</strong></li><li>Reversal of vasectomy – early rather than late.</li><li>Delayed reversal More failure due to anti Sperm Ab.</li><li>Varicocelectomy: Not for fertility treatment.</li><li>Sperm Retrieval:</li><li>Testes</li><li>TESA</li><li>TESE</li><li>Epididymis</li><li>MESA</li><li>PESA</li><li><strong>ART:</strong></li><li><em><strong>IUI</strong></em></li><li>Mild oligo</li><li>Same sex</li><li>Post testicular causes:</li><li>Ejaculatory</li><li>Erectile dysfunction.</li><li><em><strong>IVF</strong></em></li><li>Mild male factor infertility</li><li><em><strong>ICSI</strong></em></li><li>Severe form or failed fertilization in IVF</li><li>33% pregnancy rate</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Favorable Results:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Zinc</li><li>Selenium</li><li>Omega 3 FA</li><li>CO – Q10</li><li>Carotenes</li></ul>
<h3><strong>New developments in Sperm Selection in ART: </strong></h3>
<ul><li>Density gradient configuration</li><li>Swim up</li><li>MESOME:</li><li>Motile sperm organelle morphology evaluation:</li><li>Acrosome</li><li>Post acrosomal stamina</li><li>Neck</li><li>ICSI with morphologically selected sperm injection (IMSI)</li><li>PICSI – physiological ICSI</li><li>HOS – Hypo osmotic swelling</li></ul>', 3) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
