<p>F/U visit to discuss future fertilityF/U visit to discuss future fertilityF/U visit to discuss future fertilityF/U visit to discuss future fertility</p>
<h3><strong>MDT in CA:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Gynaecological oncologists.</li><li>Paedriatic oncologists.</li><li>Paedriatic surgeon.</li><li>Paedriatic and adolescent Gynaecologist</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Surgery:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Commonly by paeds surgeon with input from Gynaecologist</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Surgical tips for laparoscopy in </strong><strong>children’s</strong><strong> and Adolesants:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Bladder is intraperitoneal =&gt; problem with supra pubic port.</li><li>Urethral trauma while catheterization &lt;10 years.</li><li>Aorta just below skin in skinny children.</li><li>Lift up umbilicus before port insertion.</li><li>Pneumoperitoneum @ 12 – 15mm hg in Adolesants.</li><li>8 – 10 in children.</li><li>Port size Hernia – use 2 – 5mm port.</li><li>Close fascia &gt; 10mm port size.</li><li>Keep camera on while removing umbilical port due to risk of omental evisceration.</li><li>Avoid vaginal examination and uterine manipulation.</li><li>Limited lungs functioning due to intraperitoneal Co2 under pressure</li></ul>', 3) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
