<ul><li><strong>&gt; 35 IU/ml.TVS in P0 – CARE &gt; 35 IU/ml.TVS in P0 – CARE </strong>&gt; 35 IU/ml.<strong>TVS</strong><strong> in P</strong><strong>0 </strong><strong>– CARE </strong>&gt; 35 IU/ml.<strong>TVS</strong><strong> in P</strong><strong>0 </strong><strong>– CARE </strong></li></ul>
<p>Normal</p>
<ul><li>NormalNormalNormalNormal<strong>Suggest cancer =&gt; RMI calculationUSG abdomen + pelvisCT if USG suggests CANeoadjuvant Chemo after:Tissue Diagnosis:Percutaneous image guided biopsyLaparoscopy Guided.cytology if H/P not appropriate.Suggest cancer =&gt; RMI calculationUSG abdomen + pelvisCT if USG suggests CANeoadjuvant Chemo after:Tissue Diagnosis:Percutaneous image guided biopsyLaparoscopy Guided.cytology if H/P not appropriate.</strong><strong>Suggest cancer</strong> =&gt; RMI calculationUSG abdomen + pelvisCT if USG suggests CA<strong>Neoadjuvant</strong><strong> Chemo after:</strong>Tissue Diagnosis:Percutaneous image guided biopsyLaparoscopy Guided.cytology if H/P not appropriate.<strong>Suggest cancer</strong> =&gt; RMI calculationUSG abdomen + pelvisCT if USG suggests CA<strong>Neoadjuvant</strong><strong> Chemo after:</strong>Tissue Diagnosis:Percutaneous image guided biopsyLaparoscopy Guided.cytology if H/P not appropriate.</li><li>Assessment</li></ul>
<p>carefully.</p>
<ul><li>rule out causes</li></ul>
<p>of symptoms.</p>
<ul><li>return to GP if</li></ul>
<p>symptoms become</p>
<p>frequent/ persistent.</p>
<h3><strong>Treatment:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Surgery – full staging</li><li>Lymph node assessment, lymph node dissension</li><li>Adjuvant Chemo:</li><li>Stage I:</li><li>Grade 1 &amp; 2, Ia, Ib not recommended.</li><li>Grade 3, Ic recommended.</li><li>6 cycles of carboplatin.</li><li>Discuss Adjuvant chemo in stage I that is not optimally staged.</li></ul>', 1) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-e3579c77', 't-mm-03-009', 'html', '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>SATGE I:</strong></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>MANAGEMENT</strong></td><td><strong>5 YEARS </strong><br/><strong>SURVIVAL</strong></td><td><strong>1 YEAR</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>A</strong><br/><strong>B</strong><br/><strong>C</strong></td><td>Limited to 1 ovary capsule intact =&gt;</td><td><em><strong>Fertility </strong></em><em><strong>sparing</strong></em><em><strong> can be consisted in young:</strong></em></td><td>90%<br/>80%</td><td>98%</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Limited to both ovaries capsule intact</td><td><strong>Stating Laparotomy:</strong><br/>TAH + BSO<br/>Evaluation of all peritoneal surfaces<br/>Washings for cytology<br/>Multiple peritoneal biopsies.<br/>Omentectomy.<br/>Pelvic/para – aortic LN biopsies.<br/>Hepatic/ diaphragmatic cytology.<br/><em><strong>Cytoreductive</strong></em><em><strong> surgery:</strong></em> Residual disease<br/>&lt; 1cm.<br/><em><strong>Chemotherapy:</strong></em> carboplatin + paclitaxel = 6 cycles.<br/><em><strong>Main sta</strong></em><em><strong>y</strong></em><em><strong> of treatment:</strong></em> surgery + chemo except stage 1A,1B, low grade</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>1: 1A/1B with surgical spill<br/>2: 1A/1B with ruptured capsule before surgery or tumor on surface.<br/>3: 1A/1B but malignant cells in ascites or peritoneal washings.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>STAGE II:</strong></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>  </strong>            <strong>A</strong><br/><strong>B</strong><br/><strong>C</strong></td><td>Implants on surface of uterus, tubes, ovary.</td><td>Surgery: + Adjuvant therapy according to MDT decision.<br/>Surgery: + Neoadjuvant or adjuvant therapy according to MDT decision.</td><td>70%</td><td>89%</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Other pelvic organs Bladder, rectum.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>IIA, IIB with ascites or peritoneal washings positive</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>STAGE III:</strong></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>A</strong><strong>1</strong><br/><strong> A</strong><strong>2</strong><br/><strong>B</strong><br/><strong>C</strong></td><td>Positive Retroperitoneal Lymph nodes<br/><strong>III</strong><em><strong>A</strong></em><em><strong>1</strong></em><em><strong>a</strong></em><em><strong>:</strong></em> &lt;10mm Mets<br/><em><strong>IIIA</strong></em><em><strong>1b</strong></em><em><strong>:</strong></em> &gt; 10mm Mets – peritoneal Mets</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>40%</td><td>73%</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Microscopic extra pelvic peritoneal invasion + positive retroperitoneal Lymph nodes.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Macroscopic &lt; 2cm extra pelvic peritoneal Mets + positive retroperitoneal Lymph nodes.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Extra pelvic peritoneal Mets &gt;2cm Macroscopic, positive retroperitoneal L nodes.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Extension to liver/spleen capsule abdominal organs – No parenchymal involvement.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>STAGE: IV</strong></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>A</strong><br/><strong>B  </strong></td><td>Plural effusion with + ive cytology.</td><td>Neoadjuvant followed by surgery according to MDT decision</td><td>20%</td><td>53%<br/>Un stage – 67%.<br/>Unknown stage = 53%.</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Hepatic, splenic parenchymal Mets.<br/>Mets to extra abdominal organs.<br/>inguinal L nodes.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-71c869e1', 't-mm-03-009', 'html', '<p>Table 7. CA OVARY</p>
<h3><strong>E </strong><strong>secreting</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Granulosa cell tumors</li><li>Thecoma</li><li>50% estrogenic</li><li>40% non-functional</li><li>20% androgenic</li><li>Sertoli cell</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Androgen Secreting</strong>:</h3>
<ul><li>Andro blastoma</li><li>Adrenal like</li><li>Gonad blastoma</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Stage II, IV:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Either surgery F/B adjuvant</li><li>Or neoadjuvant.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Relapse:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Platinum sensitive- Relapse after 12m0</li><li>of completion of t/m</li><li>Partial sensitive- Between 6 – 12m0</li><li>of completion.</li><li>Resistant - &lt; 6m of completion</li><li>Refractory- Within 4 weeks or</li></ul>
<p>during treatment</p>
<p>Complete RESPONSE = 4 weeks of treatment</p>
<p><strong>Chemo:</strong>   es risk of Pre – term labour</p>
<p><strong>Radio:</strong>   es risk of miscarriage, still birth and IUGR.</p>
<h3><strong>pulmonary fibrosisHand foot syndrome, cerebellar AtaxiaNeuropathycardiac failure Hemorrhagic cystitis.Nephrotoxic, deafness.Bone marrow suppression.Neurotoxicity.Bone marrow toxicityMylo suppressionpulmonary fibrosisHand foot syndrome, cerebellar AtaxiaNeuropathycardiac failure Hemorrhagic cystitis.Nephrotoxic, deafness.Bone marrow suppression.Neurotoxicity.Bone marrow toxicityMylo suppression</strong>pulmonary fibrosisHand foot syndrome, cerebellar AtaxiaNeuropathycardiac failure Hemorrhagic cystitis.Nephrotoxic, deafness.Bone marrow suppression.Neurotoxicity.Bone marrow toxicityMylo suppressionpulmonary fibrosisHand foot syndrome, cerebellar AtaxiaNeuropathycardiac failure Hemorrhagic cystitis.Nephrotoxic, deafness.Bone marrow suppression.Neurotoxicity.Bone marrow toxicityMylo suppression<strong>Toxicity of Chemo</strong><strong>therapy</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Bleomycin</li><li>5 – fluorouracil</li><li>Paclitaxel</li><li>Doxorubicin</li><li>Cyclophosphamide</li><li>Cisplatin</li><li>Methotrexate</li><li>Vincristine</li><li>Vinblastine</li><li>Carboplatin</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Chemotherapy MOA:</strong></h3>
<p><strong>Fluor</strong><strong>o</strong><strong>uracil</strong><strong>:</strong> - inhibition of thymidylate synthase.</p>
<p><strong>Bleomyc</strong><strong>in:</strong> cause single stranded synthesis of DNA.</p>
<p><strong>Paclitaxe</strong><strong>l:</strong> prevention of microtubule assembly</p>
<p><strong>Doxo</strong><strong>rubicin</strong><strong>:</strong> Topoisomerase II inhibiter.</p>
<p><strong>Ifos</strong><strong>f</strong><strong>amide:</strong> Alkylating agent.</p>
<p><strong>Cisplatin:</strong> crosslink DNA inhibition</p>
<h3><strong>P</strong><strong>0</strong><strong> concern of comorbidities</strong><strong> before starting chemotherapy</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Bleomycin – COPD.</li><li>5 Fluorouracil – IHD.</li><li>Taxanes – Diabetes.</li><li>anthracyclines – CCF.</li><li>Methotrexate – plural effusion, Metho pools in 3rd space causing toxicity.</li></ul>
<p><strong>Paclitaxel:</strong> Given with oral dexamethasone, 20mg, 6-12 hours prior to avoid hypersensitivity reactions, It impairs blood glucose, so used with caution</p>
<p><strong>Cisplatin:</strong> pre and post hydration.</p>
<p><strong>Bleomycin:</strong> don’t cause myelosuppression.</p>
<p><strong>Etoposide:</strong> Both oral and I/V.</p>
<p><strong>Carboplatin:</strong> dosed acc to creatinine levels</p>
<h3><strong> </strong><strong>BRCA Gene:</strong></h3>', 3) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
