<p><strong>Medical therapy options for women using hormonal contraception with problematic bleedingMedical therapy options for women using hormonal contraception with problematic bleeding</strong><strong>Medical therapy options for women using hormonal contraception with problematic bleeding</strong><strong>Medical therapy options for women using hormonal contraception with problematic bleeding</strong>Medical therapy options for women using hormonal contraception with problematic bleeding.</p>
<p><strong>Progestogen only implants. Injectable or intrauterine systemProgestogen only implants. Injectable or intrauterine system</strong>Progestogen only implants. Injectable or intrauterine systemProgestogen only implants. Injectable or intrauterine system<strong>Progestogen only pill usersProgestogen only pill users</strong>Progestogen only pill usersProgestogen only pill users<strong>Combined hormonal contraception usersCombined hormonal contraception users</strong>Combined hormonal contraception usersCombined hormonal contraception users</p>
<p><strong>Could try a different POP Women may experience different bleeding with patterns was the traditional POP and the DSG POP No evidence to support the use of two POPS per day to improve bleeding Although regimens such as estrogen supplementation or tranexamic acid may help to reduce bleeding induced by progestogen-only contraceptives in the short-term evidence does not support routine use of such regimens particularly daily for long term effect.Could try a different POP Women may experience different bleeding with patterns was the traditional POP and the DSG POP No evidence to support the use of two POPS per day to improve bleeding Although regimens such as estrogen supplementation or tranexamic acid may help to reduce bleeding induced by progestogen-only contraceptives in the short-term evidence does not support routine use of such regimens particularly daily for long term effect.</strong>Could try a different POP Women may experience different bleeding with patterns was the traditional POP and the DSG POP No evidence to support the use of two POPS per day to improve bleeding Although regimens such as estrogen supplementation or tranexamic acid may help to reduce bleeding induced by progestogen-only contraceptives in the short-term evidence does not support routine use of such regimens particularly daily for long term effect.Could try a different POP Women may experience different bleeding with patterns was the traditional POP and the DSG POP No evidence to support the use of two POPS per day to improve bleeding Although regimens such as estrogen supplementation or tranexamic acid may help to reduce bleeding induced by progestogen-only contraceptives in the short-term evidence does not support routine use of such regimens particularly daily for long term effect.<strong>In general, continue with the same pill for at least 3 months’ as bleeding may settle in this time. Use COC with a dose of EE to provide the best cycle control Could consider increasing the EE