<ul><li>HIP Buttock and Back Pain</li><li>Doppler, MR, venography, contrast venography.</li><li>DVT Pts – 15 – 24% develops PE, 50% had underlays thrombophilia.</li><li>PE mortality 15% (66% within 30 min).</li><li>ECG – S, Q3T3 pattern RBB 18%.</li><li>CXR – rule out pneumonia, pneumothorax, lobar collapse.</li><li>ABG’S – nonspecific.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>CTPA.</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Readily available.</li><li>Fetal exposure.</li><li>Radiation exposure to Breast.</li><li>14% risk of CA Breast.</li><li>Done with abnormal CxR.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>V/Q Scan:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Exposure to breast tissue.</li><li>Done in young women with family history of CA Breast &amp; who had previous chest CT scan.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Treatment: DVT</strong></h3>
<ul><li>LMWH – till 6 weeks of delivery or total 3 months.</li><li>Factor x – a activity not recommended except</li><li>1.Extremes of BMI &lt;50kg, &gt;100kg.</li><li>2.Abnormal RFT’s</li><li>3.Recurrent DVT.</li></ul>', 1) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
