<h3><strong>Referral to FMU:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Anti D &gt; 4, Anti C &gt;7.5, Any anti K.</li><li>Significant history of HDFN requiring exchange Tx, unexplained severe jaundice, titer of &gt; 32.</li><li>Rising titer.</li><li>USG suggestive of fetal anemia.</li><li>Other than C, D, K (any titer).</li><li>MCA PSV &gt;1.5MOM | Signs of anemia.</li><li>Need for IUT</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Causes of Alloimmunization</strong></h3>
<p>should be ascertained</p>
<ul><li>Blood Tx.</li><li>Inadequate Anti D/ omitted Anti D injections.</li><li>IUT, exchange Tx, Severe jaundice requiring phototherapy.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>MCA – PSV: </strong></h3>
<ul><li>Weekly by expert</li><li>Sensitivity 99%.</li><li>False positive 12%.</li><li>Sensitivity    after 36 weeks.</li><li>1.5 MOM =&gt; referral to FMU for FBS – (loss rate = 1 – 3% FBS).</li></ul>
<h3><strong>IUT:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>O negative D-ve, O+ve, C-ve, K-ve</li><li>CMV negative.</li><li>Citrate phosphate dextrose.</li><li>&lt; 5 days old.</li><li>HCT = 0.70 – 0.85.</li><li>Irradiated within 24 hours</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Ex</strong><strong>change</strong><strong> Tx: </strong></h3>
<ul><li>HCT 0.5 – 0.6.</li><li>Group specific.</li><li>Ab negative, K-ve.</li><li>CMV negative. &lt; 5 days old.</li><li>Irradiated.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Top – Up:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>35 days old.</li><li>Non – irradiated.</li><li>Irradiation only if IUT already given.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>High Risk women </strong><strong>for</strong><strong> Tx:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Weekly cross matching.</li><li>Sample should not be &gt;12hrs old.</li></ul>
<p>Used- same group ABO.</p>
