<h3><strong>Risk of congenital </strong><strong>sequalae &amp; complications</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Early = 85%.</li><li>Late = 10 – 80%.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Mother to child transmission:</strong></h3>', 1) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-d00fb5fa', 't-mm-09-010', 'html', '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>trimester</strong></td><td><strong>CMV</strong></td><td><strong>Risk of </strong><strong>Toxo</strong></td></tr><tr><td>1st</td><td>40%</td><td>10%</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>40%</td><td>25%</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>80%</td><td>&gt; 85%</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-1ad2a0a3', 't-mm-09-010', 'html', '<h3><strong>Toxo Triad:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Intra cerebral calcifications.</li><li>Hydrocephaly.</li><li>Chorioretinitis.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Diagnosis:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Routine screening not recommended.</li><li>Serial USG to detect markers</li><li>Ascites.</li><li>Hepatosplenomegaly.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Tests:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>ELIZA = enzyme – linked immune filtration assay.</li><li>PCR of amniotic fluid is highly accurate.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Implications:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Miscarriages.</li><li>Ascites/ hepatosplenomegaly.</li><li>Chorioretinitis.</li><li>Hydrocephaly.</li><li>Brain tissue calcification.</li><li>Visual impairment of fetus.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Management:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Antiparasitic – prevent fetal damage after transmission.</li><li>Not possible to eradicate.</li><li>TOP is an option.</li><li>Spiramycin to prevent congenital infections.</li><li>Sulphadiazine/ pyrimethamine given only if infection is confirmed (can be toxic).</li></ul>', 3) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO topics (id, chapter_id, title, description, `order`, is_published, author, source) VALUES ('t-mm-09-011', 'chap-mm-09-01', '1.10.RUBELLA', 'Detailed medical reference and study guide on 1.10.RUBELLA.', 11, true, 'Dr. Farzana Muneer', 'Maternal Mind FCPS/MRCOG Textbook') ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE title=VALUES(title), description=VALUES(description), is_published=true;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-cc057fd8', 't-mm-09-011', 'html', '<ul><li>P0 Rubella</li><li>16/52 weeks – substantial.</li><li>Top</li><li>16 – 20 weeks – minimal risk</li><li>Follow up</li><li>After 20 weeks – no risk</li><li>Reassure.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Congenital Rubella symptoms:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Sensory neural deafness.</li><li>PDA, VSD.</li><li>Eye lesions, cataract, micro Ophthalmia.</li><li>Microcephaly.</li><li>Mental retardation.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Implications of Rubella to Fetus/ Neonate:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>SN – deafness.</li><li>DM.</li><li>Thyroid disease.</li><li>GH deficiency.</li><li>Vascular effects</li><li>encephalitis.</li></ul>', 1) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO topics (id, chapter_id, title, description, `order`, is_published, author, source) VALUES ('t-mm-09-012', 'chap-mm-09-01', '1.11.SYPHILIS', 'Detailed medical reference and study guide on 1.11.SYPHILIS.', 12, true, 'Dr. Farzana Muneer', 'Maternal Mind FCPS/MRCOG Textbook') ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE title=VALUES(title), description=VALUES(description), is_published=true;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-99f41b65', 't-mm-09-012', 'html', '<ul><li>70 cases/ million deliveries.</li><li>Treponema pallidum.</li><li>Transmission:</li><li>Direct contact with lesion.</li><li>Vertical transmission.</li><li>Universal screening.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Course of syphilis:</strong></h3>
<ul><li><em><strong>Early:</strong></em></li><li>P0: maculopapular rash + regional lymphadenopathy 10 days – 3m0.</li><li>Chancre, anogenital region, hard – indurated.</li><li>Secondary: untreated primary lesions.</li><li>25% sec syphilis after 4 – 10 weeks.</li><li>Multisystem involvement.</li><li>Rash + generalized lymphadenopathy.</li><li><em><strong>Latent Asymptomatic:</strong></em></li><li>Early – within 2 years.</li><li>Late – after 2 years.</li><li><em><strong>Late:</strong></em></li><li>Tertiary, Quarterly.</li><li>Gumas, system involvement:</li><li>CVS</li><li>CNS</li><li>Tabes dorsalis</li><li>General paresis.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Diagnosis:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Best test: TPHA, EIA.</li><li>Screening: VDRL.</li><li>Microscopic identification.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>USG:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Early onset SGA:</li><li>TORCH screening.</li><li>Karyotyping.</li><li>FGR.</li><li>Brain:</li><li>Calcification.</li><li>Hydrocephaly.</li><li>Hydro anencephaly</li><li>Microcephaly.</li><li>GI:</li><li>Abnormal liver, spleen, bowels.</li><li>Ascites, hepatosplenomegaly.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Congenital syphilis:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Hydrops.</li><li>Nasal bone depressed, saddle nose.</li><li>Rash.</li><li>Hepatosplenomegaly.</li><li>Petechial rash.</li><li>Weinberger sign.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Neonatal:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Untreated – 50% dies.</li><li>Frontal bossing.</li><li>Saddle nose.</li><li>Interstitial keratitis.</li><li>Rhagades.</li><li>Perforated hard palate.</li><li>Hutchinson teeth.</li><li>Mulberry molar.</li><li>Saber shins.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Fetal implications:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Before 16 weeks – rare.</li><li>Miscarriage.</li><li>Still birth.</li><li>Neonatal death, disease or latent infection.</li><li>Untreated syphilis =&gt; 50% loss.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Treatment of syphilis:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Non – pregnant.</li><li>Pregnant.</li><li><em><strong>Non – pregnant:</strong></em></li><li><strong>Early:</strong></li><li>Benzathine penicillin G 2.4MU I/m x Stat single dose.</li><li>Amoxicillin 2mg P/o TDS</li><li>+ probenecid 500mg QDS</li><li>Ceftriaxone 2g I/M or I/V 10 – 14 days.</li><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong></li><li><strong>Early syphilis:</strong></li></ul>
<p>Up to 28 days.After 28 days.</p>
<p>Penicillin G 2.4MU I/m.double dose</p>
<p>Single dose.Day 1</p>
<p>Day 8</p>
<h3><strong>Late syphilis</strong><strong> in pregnancy</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Late latent/Gumas/CVS/CNS.</li><li><strong>Doses</strong></li><li>Day 1, 8, 15.</li><li><strong>Neurosyphilis</strong></li><li><strong>Procaine</strong><strong> penicillin</strong> G</li><li>1.8 – 2.4 MU OD<strong>14 days.</strong></li><li>Plus</li><li><strong>Probenecid 500mg QDS.</strong></li><li>Benzyl Penicillin</li><li>10.8 – 14.4 daily.</li><li>1.8 – 2.4 I/V every 4 hours for 14 days.</li></ul>', 1) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO topics (id, chapter_id, title, description, `order`, is_published, author, source) VALUES ('t-mm-09-013', 'chap-mm-09-01', '1.12.PARVOVIRUS', 'Detailed medical reference and study guide on 1.12.PARVOVIRUS.', 13, true, 'Dr. Farzana Muneer', 'Maternal Mind FCPS/MRCOG Textbook') ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE title=VALUES(title), description=VALUES(description), is_published=true;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-133b6d0d', 't-mm-09-013', 'html', '<ul><li>Incubation period 4 – 14 days.</li><li>DNA – virus single stranded DNA.</li><li>Spontaneous replication in diving cells (S – phase).</li><li>Replicate and inhibit CFU &amp; cause lysis of human erythroid progenitor cells.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Transmission:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Droplets borne:</li><li>50 – 90% house hold contact.</li><li>20 – 30% in school staff.</li></ul>
<p><strong>Out Breaks: </strong>in spring.</p>
<p>50% of child bearing are immune.</p>
<ul><li>Vertical transmission 30% (so TOP not indicated).</li><li>1% of susceptible individuals are infected /year, 1 infection /400 pregnancy, 23 times higher during epidemics.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Fetal risks:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Loss rate 9% highest in 2nd .</li></ul>', 1) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-e5308e1d', 't-mm-09-013', 'image', '/uploads/content-images/maternal_mind_book/image124.emf', 2) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-8b981440', 't-mm-09-013', 'html', '<ul><li>Hydrops 3% commonest finding (10 – 20% of non – immune hydrops).</li><li>Reticulocytosis (&gt; 20% Good prognostic sign)</li><li>spontaneous recovery 34%</li><li>IUD &lt;10% after 4 – 6weeks.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Diagnosis:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>IgM (3 days – 6m0).</li><li>Pregnancy + rash + arthralgia.</li><li>Exposure history.</li><li>Non – immune hydrops.</li><li>IUD.</li><li>History, examination.</li><li>Counselling + decision to investigate.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>A/N Booking serum</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Not availableTake sample for igG + IgM when rash appears or 21 days after exposure.Not availableTake sample for igG + IgM when rash appears or 21 days after exposure.Not availableTake sample for igG + IgM when rash appears or 21 days after exposure.Not availableTake sample for igG + IgM when rash appears or 21 days after exposure.</li></ul>
<p>Available</p>
<p>Sero positiveSero negative</p>
<ul><li>IgM positiveInfectedRefer to specialistUSG for fetal anemiaIUT if neededIgM positiveInfectedRefer to specialistUSG for fetal anemiaIUT if neededIgM positiveInfectedRefer to specialistUSG for fetal anemiaIUT if neededIgM positiveInfectedRefer to specialistUSG for fetal anemiaIUT if neededIgG negativeIgM negativeSusceptle but not infectedF/uIgG negativeIgM negativeSusceptle but not infectedF/uIgG negativeIgM negativeSusceptle but not infectedF/uIgG negativeIgM negativeSusceptle but not infectedF/uIgG positiveIgM negativeIgG positiveIgM negativeIgG positiveIgM negativeIgG positiveIgM negativeReassure</li></ul>
<p>No risk</p>
<ul><li>Serial USG for up to 12 weeks after confirmed infection.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Treatment:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Maternal – symptomatic treatment.</li><li>Hydrops – FMU referral.</li><li>Delivery if Gestation is appropriate.</li><li>FBS with conservative management if reticulocytosis positive.</li><li>IUT if anemia on FBS</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Transmission:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>&lt; 15 weeks = 15%.</li><li>15 – 20 weeks = 25%.</li><li>Last  = 70%.</li></ul>', 3) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE content=VALUES(content), type=VALUES(type);
