<h3><strong>Risk factors:</strong></h3>
<ul><li><em><strong>Procedure related:Half of cord prolapse (are procedure related)1.  ARM with high presenting part2.  Vaginal manipulation with ruptured membranes Avoid upward pushing3. ECV4. Stabilizing induction5. Insertion of I/U Catheter Esp if filled more than 180ml.Procedure related:Half of cord prolapse (are procedure related)1.  ARM with high presenting part2.  Vaginal manipulation with ruptured membranes Avoid upward pushing3. ECV4. Stabilizing induction5. Insertion of I/U Catheter Esp if filled more than 180ml.</strong></em><em><strong>Procedure related:</strong></em>Half of cord prolapse (are procedure related)1.  ARM with high presenting part2.  Vaginal manipulation with ruptured membranes Avoid upward pushing3. ECV4. Stabilizing induction5. Insertion of I/U Catheter Esp if filled more than 180ml.<em><strong>Procedure related:</strong></em>Half of cord prolapse (are procedure related)1.  ARM with high presenting part2.  Vaginal manipulation with ruptured membranes Avoid upward pushing3. ECV4. Stabilizing induction5. Insertion of I/U Catheter Esp if filled more than 180ml.</li></ul>
